-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ט/7: עדכונים בנושא פדיון עבור ימי מחלה בלתי מנוצלים
-- Changes, under the Treasury's instructions of 4.11.2008, 21.12.2008 and
-- 21.1.2009, to the compensation for unused sick days: an early retiree who
-- goes on to teach for another employer in the education system is
-- compensated for the sick days accrued there; and the continuity of
-- section 13 of the agreements of 11.5.1993 extends to an employee who moved
-- employer and received only a severance-pay top-up.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `תשס"ט/7 עדכונים בנושא פדיון עבור ימי מחלה בלתי מנוצלים`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, date (30.4.2009), addressee, greeting, subject line, and the lead-in: under the Treasury's instructions of 4.11.08, 21.12.08 and 21.1.09, the changes below; remarks in square brackets are the Ministry of Education's. No rule of its own.

-- Time: a school year is named by the calendar year it ends in, so תשס"ח
-- (September 2007 to August 2008) is 2008.

@desc The employers the section 1 examples move between.
DECLARE `employer kind` IS ONE OF
    `the State`
    `an owner`

@desc A teaching employee's retirement and later employment, as far as this circular asks about them.
DECLARE `retiree` HAS
    `school year of retirement`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the school year in which the employee retired, named by the calendar year it ends in (תשס"ח = 2008)
    `retired at the end of the school year`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc the retirement took effect at the end of that school year
    `retired on early pension`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `was compensated for unused sick days on retiring` IS A BOOLEAN @desc whether or not, it does not matter to section 1
    `former employer`                        IS AN `employer kind`
    `now teaches for another employer in the education system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `new employer`                           IS AN `employer kind`
    `meets the owner agreement's conditions for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc meets the conditions of entitlement to compensation at an owner under the collective agreement on the subject; an input of that agreement
    `meets every condition of the compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc every condition that applies to the compensation for unused sick days; an input of those rules
    `sick days accrued at the new employer`  IS A NUMBER
    `sick days accrued at the former employer` IS A NUMBER

@desc A teaching employee who moved from employer to employer, as section 2 asks.
DECLARE `employee who moved` HAS
    `school year of the move`                IS A NUMBER  @desc named by the calendar year it ends in
    `moved at the end of the school year`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `received only a severance-pay top-up`   IS A BOOLEAN @desc on moving, received only a top-up of severance pay
    `severance received as a share of statutory severance` IS A NUMBER @desc the severance received, as a share of severance pay under the Severance Pay Law 1963 (1 = 100%)

`the first school year of the change` MEANS 2008

§§ `1 פיצוי בגין ימי מחלה לפורש לפנסיה מוקדמת שעבר למעסיק אחר`

-- The start of the change, as section 1 and section 2א print it twice:
-- the rule ("החל משנת הלימודים תשס"ח", from school year 2007/08) and the
-- Ministry's bracketed gloss ("כלומר: ... שפרש בסוף שנת הלימודים תשס"ח
-- ואילך", who retired at the end of 2007/08 or later). They differ for a
-- retirement during 2007/08 before its end (F-2008-09_tashsat_07-a).
GIVEN `school year` IS A NUMBER, `at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the change by the rule's words` `school year` `at the end of the year` IF
    `school year` AT LEAST `the first school year of the change`

GIVEN `school year` IS A NUMBER, `at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the change by the Ministry's gloss` `school year` `at the end of the year` IF
        `school year` GREATER THAN `the first school year of the change`
    OR (`school year` EQUALS `the first school year of the change` AND `at the end of the year`)

-- The reading adopted (F-2008-09_tashsat_07-a): the Ministry's gloss, which
-- says what the owners are to apply — the change starts with retirements at
-- the end of 2007/08.
GIVEN `school year` IS A NUMBER, `at the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the change` `school year` `at the end of the year` IF
    `within the change by the Ministry's gloss` `school year` `at the end of the year`

-- Section 1: an employee who retired on early pension (compensated for
-- unused sick days on retiring or not) and went on to be employed as a
-- teaching employee by another employer in the education system is entitled
-- to compensation for unused sick days — provided, the Ministry adds, he
-- meets the conditions at an owner under the collective agreement — for the
-- sick days accrued at that other employer alone, subject to every condition
-- of the compensation (an input of those rules).
@ref akn:art_1/p1
GIVEN r IS A `retiree`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to compensation for sick days at the new employer` r IF
        `within the change` (r's `school year of retirement`) (r's `retired at the end of the school year`)
    AND r's `retired on early pension`
    AND r's `now teaches for another employer in the education system`
    AND r's `meets the owner agreement's conditions for compensation`
    AND r's `meets every condition of the compensation`

GIVEN r IS A `retiree`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days the compensation is for` r IS
    IF `entitled to compensation for sick days at the new employer` r
    THEN r's `sick days accrued at the new employer`
    ELSE 0

-- The Ministry's examples (section 1, in brackets): a State employee who
-- went to an owner, an owner's employee who went to the State, and an
-- employee who went from one owner to another — compensated or not on
-- retiring. Each is a move between two employers of the education system.
@ref akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_b akn:art_1__para_c
`the examples' moves` MEANS
    LIST `move between employers` `the State` `an owner`,
         `move between employers` `an owner` `the State`,
         `move between employers` `an owner` `an owner`

DECLARE `move between employers` HAS
    `moved from` IS AN `employer kind`
    `moved to`   IS AN `employer kind`

-- Section 1, closing bracket: in the examples the employee is entitled to
-- compensation for the unused sick days he accrues with the second employer
-- alone, subject to every condition on the subject.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c/p2
GIVEN r IS A `retiree`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the days at the former employer are not counted` r IF
    `sick days the compensation is for` r AT MOST r's `sick days accrued at the new employer`

§§ `2 רציפות בגין ימי מחלה בלתי מנוצלים`

-- Section 2א: from 2007/08 (the same rule and gloss as section 1), section
-- 13 of the collective agreements of 11.5.1993 — continuity of unused sick
-- days — applies also to an employee who moved from employer to employer and
-- received only a severance-pay top-up, up to 100% of severance pay under the
-- Severance Pay Law 1963. What section 13 then gives is that agreement's.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN m IS AN `employee who moved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 13's continuity extends to` m IF
        `within the change` (m's `school year of the move`) (m's `moved at the end of the school year`)
    AND m's `received only a severance-pay top-up`
    AND m's `severance received as a share of statutory severance` AT MOST 1

-- Section 2ב: nothing in the section changes the other rules on
-- compensation for unused sick days. The rule above is the only thing it
-- adds; the rest is those rules', an input here.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
`section 2 changes no other rule on unused sick days` MEANS TRUE


-- akn:art_3 The indemnity procedure for the subject will be updated and sent separately; nothing is decided here.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- F-2008-09_tashsat_07-a: a retirement during 2007/08, before its end, is
-- within the change by the rule's words and outside it by the gloss.
`the rule and its gloss differ for a retirement during 2007/08` MEANS
        `within the change by the rule's words` 2008 FALSE
    AND (NOT (`within the change by the Ministry's gloss` 2008 FALSE))
#ASSERT `the rule and its gloss differ for a retirement during 2007/08`

`an early retiree from the State teaching at an owner since 2008` MEANS
    `retiree` WITH
        `school year of retirement`              IS 2008
        `retired at the end of the school year`  IS TRUE
        `retired on early pension`               IS TRUE
        `was compensated for unused sick days on retiring` IS TRUE
        `former employer`                        IS `the State`
        `now teaches for another employer in the education system` IS TRUE
        `new employer`                           IS `an owner`
        `meets the owner agreement's conditions for compensation` IS TRUE
        `meets every condition of the compensation` IS TRUE
        `sick days accrued at the new employer`  IS 40
        `sick days accrued at the former employer` IS 200

`an early retiree who left in the middle of 2007/08` MEANS
    `retiree` WITH
        `school year of retirement`              IS 2008
        `retired at the end of the school year`  IS FALSE
        `retired on early pension`               IS TRUE
        `was compensated for unused sick days on retiring` IS FALSE
        `former employer`                        IS `an owner`
        `now teaches for another employer in the education system` IS TRUE
        `new employer`                           IS `an owner`
        `meets the owner agreement's conditions for compensation` IS TRUE
        `meets every condition of the compensation` IS TRUE
        `sick days accrued at the new employer`  IS 40
        `sick days accrued at the former employer` IS 200

#ASSERT `sick days the compensation is for` `an early retiree from the State teaching at an owner since 2008` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the days at the former employer are not counted` `an early retiree from the State teaching at an owner since 2008`
#ASSERT `sick days the compensation is for` `an early retiree who left in the middle of 2007/08` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT count `the examples' moves` EQUALS 3

`a teacher who moved with a severance top-up` MEANS
    `employee who moved` WITH
        `school year of the move`                IS 2009
        `moved at the end of the school year`    IS TRUE
        `received only a severance-pay top-up`   IS TRUE
        `severance received as a share of statutory severance` IS 1

#ASSERT `section 13's continuity extends to` `a teacher who moved with a severance top-up`
#ASSERT `section 2 changes no other rule on unused sick days`
